#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iio-interface.md:2
msgid "iio interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iio-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"`iio` enables access to a specific IIO (Industrial I/O) device. This "
"interface is restricted because it provides privileged access to IIO "
"hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iio-interface.md:6
msgid "**Auto-Connect**: no **Attributes:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iio-interface.md:8
msgid "`path` (slot): path to IIO device node e.g. `/dev/iio:device0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iio-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"Available IIO devices for the system can be seen with `snap connections`. "
"Once connected, the consuming snap can use the device via the path specified "
"by the connected slot."
msgstr ""
